# Ad-hoc credential scratch files (ACBP-API-011, 2026-08-19).
#
# A real Anthropic key was pasted into a root-level `API Key.txt` while wiring the model provider. It was never
# committed — but only because nobody ran `git add -A` in the window it existed. Nothing was stopping them:
# the file was untracked and UN-IGNORED, and `check-secrets.mjs` could not see it either, because its content
# scan covers `apps/ packages/ tools/ .github/` plus five NAMED root config files, and an arbitrary root-level
# `.txt` is in neither set.
#
# `*.key` above already covers `foo.key`; it does NOT cover the way a human actually saves one — a `.txt` on the
# desktop or at the repo root, named in plain English. These patterns cover that. The scanner gap is closed
# separately, in `tools/check-secrets.mjs`, because an ignore rule only protects the names it predicted.
*[Kk]ey.txt
*[Kk]eys.txt
*[Ss]ecret.txt
*[Ss]ecrets.txt
*[Tt]oken.txt
*[Cc]redentials.txt
API*.txt
api-key*
apikey*

